    "text": "In a series LCR circuit, the inductive reactance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and the capacitive reactance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></math> in the circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The power factor of the circuit is :",
